 one object's bounding box.\n\n**Construction**\n1. Find the non-background objects.\n2. For each one, set its bounding box with a 1-cell margin removed to background.\n3. Emit one stage per hollowed rectangle, then emit the final grid.\n\nA rectangle that is 2 or fewer cells thick has no interior, so it stays unchanged.\n\n**Applying it to the test**\nThe test has five rectangles. Each is at least 3×3, so each gets a hole:\n- 8 (3×6) → 1×4 hole\n- 6 (3×4) → 1×2 hole\n- 4 (7×6) → 5×4 hole\n- 1 (6×8) → 4×6 hole\n- 3 (3×5) → 1×3 hole","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    bg = background(g)\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        if y1 - y0 >= 2 and x1 - x0 >= 2:\n            g[y0 + 1:y1, x0 + 1:x1] = bg\n            emit(g, f\"Hollow the colour-{o['colour']} rectangle at box {o['box']}: its interior becomes background, leaving a 1-cell frame.\")\n    emit(g, \"All rectangles are now hollow frames.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"A rectangle that is 2 or fewer cells thick has no interior, so it stays unchanged."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Its interior, meaning every cell not on the rectangle's outer border, is set to background."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 1: the 4×5 red block keeps only its 1-cell frame, so a 2×3 hole appears."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each is at least 3×3, so each gets a hole:"}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- In each output, every rectangle keeps its colour and its bounding box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"lour change anywhere is object colour → 0, and every changed cell lies strictly inside one object's bounding box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"For each one, set its bounding box with a 1-cell margin removed to background."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha